§ `s 17 -- c024: Chloe at the State election of 13 March 2021, the day before her 18th birthday`

#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to be enrolled` `Chloe before enrolling` (Date 13 3 2021)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be enrolled` `Chloe before enrolling` (Date 14 3 2021)

#ASSERT `On what day did I become entitled to be enrolled` `Chloe before enrolling` EQUALS (Date 14 3 2021)

-- Even had she been enrolled at 17, she is not an elector and may not vote until 18 (s 17AA(2)).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an elector` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 13 3 2021)

#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to vote` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 13 3 2021)

-- Nor can she enrol on the day and vote provisionally: s 17(2)(a) needs s 17(1)(b), age 18.
#ASSERT NOT `Can I enrol on polling day and vote provisionally` `Chloe before enrolling` (Date 13 3 2021) TRUE

§ `s 17(1)(c), (2), (3) -- the month in the district; enrolling on polling day (HYPOTHETICAL newcomer; c046 had Chloe not enrolled)`

#ASSERT `On what day did I become entitled to be enrolled` `a newcomer to the district` EQUALS (Date 20 3 2025)

#ASSERT `Can I enrol on polling day and vote provisionally` `Chloe before enrolling` (Date 8 3 2025) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I enrol on polling day and vote provisionally` `Chloe before enrolling` (Date 8 3 2025) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I enrol on polling day and vote provisionally` `a newcomer to the district` (Date 8 3 2025) TRUE

-- Read alone, s 17(1)(e) gives no vote once the elector has left the district; the elector must enrol for the new one.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to vote` `an elector who moved out of the district` (Date 8 3 2025)

#ASSERT `Must I enrol` `an elector who moved out of the district` (Date 8 3 2025)

§ `s 18 -- people barred`

#ASSERT `Am I barred from voting` `a prisoner serving 2 years`

#ASSERT `Am I barred from enrolment` `a person off the Commonwealth roll for cognitive impairment`

#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to vote` `a prisoner serving 2 years` (Date 8 3 2025)
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to vote` `a pre-1984 British subject` (Date 8 3 2025)

#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to be enrolled` `a temporary visa holder` (Date 8 3 2025)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to be enrolled` `a person off the Commonwealth roll for cognitive impairment` (Date 8 3 2025)

§ `s 17AA -- enrolment at 16 and 17, from 1 July 2024`

-- Chloe at 17 (14 March 2020) enrolled federally (Commonwealth s 100); the deposited State text gives her no such right then.
#ASSERT NOT `May I enrol at 16 or 17` `Chloe before enrolling` (Date 14 3 2020)
#ASSERT `May I enrol at 16 or 17` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 1 7 2024)

#ASSERT `Am I taken to be a silent elector because of my age` `Jake enrolled` (Date 1 8 2024)

§ `s 45(1), (4), (5), (7) -- compulsory enrolment: Jake turns 18 on 30 August 2024 and does not enrol`

#ASSERT `Must I enrol` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 30 8 2024)
#ASSERT NOT `Must I enrol` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 29 8 2024)

-- The 21 days begin on the day of entitlement: the last day is 19 September 2024 (Commonwealth: 20 September).
#ASSERT `What is the last day by which I must be enrolled` `Jake not enrolled` EQUALS (JUST (Date 19 9 2024))
#ASSERT `What is the last day by which I must be enrolled` `a temporary visa holder` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed the offence of not being enrolled` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 19 9 2024) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of not being enrolled` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 20 9 2024) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed the offence of not being enrolled` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 20 9 2024) FALSE TRUE

-- Still unenrolled at the State election of 8 March 2025; a claim lodged with the AEC later bars proceedings (k045: enrolled by 2029).
#ASSERT `Can I be prosecuted for not being enrolled` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I be prosecuted for not being enrolled` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 45(2), (5), (8) -- a new address in the same district (HYPOTHETICAL move on 1 February 2025)`

#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my new address` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS (Date 22 2 2025)

#ASSERT NOT `Can I be prosecuted for not notifying my new address` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 22 2 2025) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be prosecuted for not notifying my new address` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 23 2 2025) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I be prosecuted for not notifying my new address` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) FALSE TRUE

§ `ss 31, 31A, 35A -- the Commonwealth roll and the State register`

#ASSERT `Does my Commonwealth enrolment reach the State register` `by my own claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my claim is also my State claim, received by the Australian Electoral Officer`
#ASSERT `Does my Commonwealth enrolment reach the State register` `by my own claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing reaches it: I must send a State claim`
#ASSERT `Does my Commonwealth enrolment reach the State register` `directly by the Australian Electoral Commission under Commonwealth section 103A or 103B` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Electoral Commissioner may enrol me on the notified information`

§ `s 156(1), (1A), (16) -- c046: Chloe's first State election (8 March 2025); k045: Jake does not vote (8 March 2029)`

#ASSERT `Must I vote` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) `voted`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I vote` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 13 3 2021) `did not vote`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I vote` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) `outside the State, and the Commissioner is satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I vote` `a prisoner serving 2 years` (Date 8 3 2025) `did not vote`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I vote` `Jake not enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) `did not vote`
#ASSERT `Must I vote` `Jake enrolled` (Date 8 3 2029) `did not vote`

#ASSERT `Do I have a valid and sufficient reason` `abstained as a religious duty`

#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of failing to vote` `Jake enrolled` (Date 8 3 2029) `did not vote`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed the offence of failing to vote` `Jake enrolled` (Date 8 3 2029) `abstained as a religious duty`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I committed the offence of failing to vote` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) `voted`

§ `s 156(2), (4), (5) -- the penalty notice (k045)`

#ASSERT `Must I be sent a penalty notice` `Jake enrolled` (Date 8 3 2029) `did not vote`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I be sent a penalty notice` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) `voted`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I be sent a penalty notice` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) `outside the State, and the Commissioner is satisfied`
#ASSERT `Must I be sent a penalty notice` `Chloe enrolled` (Date 8 3 2025) `outside the State, but the Commissioner is not satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I be sent a penalty notice` `a prisoner serving 2 years` (Date 8 3 2025) `did not vote, and the Commissioner is satisfied of something`

§ `s 156(7), (8), (13) -- k045: Jake's first State matter; his federal $20 is not under this section`

#ASSERT `What is the most the modified penalty can be` FALSE EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What is the most the modified penalty can be` TRUE EQUALS 75

#ASSERT `Is the response date lawful` (Date 1 5 2029) (Date 22 5 2029)
#ASSERT NOT `Is the response date lawful` (Date 1 5 2029) (Date 21 5 2029)

§ `s 156(11)-(15A) -- k045: what follows the notice`

#ASSERT `Does my response stop a prosecution` `I paid the modified penalty by the response date`
#ASSERT NOT `Does my response stop a prosecution` `no response by the response date`

#ASSERT `May I be sent an infringement notice` `no response by the response date`
#ASSERT NOT `May I be sent an infringement notice` `a reason, and the Commissioner is satisfied`

#ASSERT `Can I be prosecuted for failing to vote` TRUE `no response by the response date` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I be prosecuted for failing to vote` TRUE `no response by the response date` TRUE

#ASSERT `May another elector respond for me` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `Must my name be removed from the register` TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 45, 156(16), (16A) -- the fines`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `failing to vote, s 156(16)` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `a false or misleading response to a notice, s 156(16A)` EQUALS 1000

